   ENDF/B-VII Evaluation, January 2015, B. W. Sleaford (LLNL)      925 1451
            R. F. Firestone (LBNL)                                 925 1451
The prompt gamma-ray spectrum for thermal radiative capture        925 1451
(MF12 MT102) has been updated with new experimental data [Fi07],   925 1451
[IAEA07]. This entailed installing new capture lines and scaling   925 1451
the yields using the total thermal cross section in (MF 3  MT 102) 925 1451
to conserve total decay energy compared to the thermal Q value.    925 1451
File 15 continuum Spectra above 200 keV had errors corrected but   925 1451
were left unchanged otherwise.                                     925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
 ****************************************************************  925 1451
   ENDF/B-VII: Only high quality covariance data were migrated     925 1451
               from ENDF/B-VI.8 (M. Herman)                        925 1451
               For the remaining reaction channels, namely elastic 925 1451
               scattering and radiative capture, covariances were  925 1451
               estimated at LANL based on a brief analysis of      925 1451
               experimental data and their agreement with the      925 1451
               ENDF/B-VII.0 central values.                        925 1451
 ****************************************************************  925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
Reevaluation of the F-19 resonance parameters in the energy range  925 1451
up 1 MeV done by  L. C. Leal, H. Derrien (and) N. M. Greene (ORNL) 925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
Reevalaution of the F-19 cross sections up to 1 MeV.  Resoanance   925 1451
parameters were obtained with the computer code SAMMY by           925 1451
fitting three transmission measurements of Larson with thicknesses 925 1451
of 0.13093 at/b, 0.016886 at/b, and 0.024184 at/b, respectively,   925 1451
measured on the 80-m flight path at the Oak Ridge Linear (ORELA)   925 1451
Accelerator, one capture cross section of Guber measure up to      925 1451
700 keV and one inelastic cross section measumrement of Broder up  925 1451
to 1 MeV. The result of the resonance analysis is a set of         925 1451
resonance parameters containing thirty-five resonances which one   925 1451
resonance is negative to account for the bound levels and three    925 1451
lies above the cutoff energy of 1 MeV to account for the effect    925 1451
for the truncated resonances above 1 MeV. The 31 resonances in the 925 1451
the energy range up to 1 MeV are 2 s-wave, 5 p-wave, 17 d-wave,    925 1451
and 7 f-wave.  In the energy up 1 MeV F-19 has inelastic channels  925 1451
starting at the energies 109.9 keV with spin 1/2- and 197.2 keV    925 1451
with spin 5/2+.  These two channels were included in the Reich-    925 1451
Moore evalaution with SAMMY. At the present time, cross section    925 1451
processing codes do not have capability to include inelastic       925 1451
channels.  Therefore, the evaluation presented here is the         925 1451
pointwise cross section processed with SAMMY.  The resonance       925 1451
parameters evaluation will be released  as soon as the processing  925 1451
codes are able to process Reich-Moore parameters with inelastic    925 1451
channels.                                                          925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
The cross sections at 300 K at thermal are the following:          925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
                   Total    3.7496 b                               925 1451
                   Scatting 3.7400 b                               925 1451
                   Capture  9.5784-3 b                             925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
 ****************************************************************  925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
 ENDF/B-VI MOD 1 Evaluation, June 1990, Z.X.Zhao, C.Y. Fu,         925 1451
                 D.C. Larson (ORNL)                                925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
 This evaluation is based on measured data available on csisrs     925 1451
 and a theoretical calculation using the TNG statistical and       925 1451
 precompound theory code [SH86,FU88].                              925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
 FILE 2. RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                      925 1451
   SECTION 151 Only scattering length [KO79] is given.             925 1451
 FILE 3.  NEUTRON CROSS SECTION                                    925 1451
   SECTION 1.  TOTAL INTERACTION                                   925 1451
     1.0E-05 to 10 eV: Sum of free atom scattering cross           925 1451
       section and the capture cross section.                      925 1451
     10 Ev to 2.0 MeV: Calculated from a set of resonance          925 1451
     parameters which were adjusted to fit the high                925 1451
     resolution measured total cross sections [LA76] by            925 1451
     using the SAMMY multi-level R-matrix analysis code [LA87].    925 1451
     2.0 MeV to 20 MeV: The values of ENDF/B-V are used.           925 1451
   SECTION 2.  ELASTIC SCATTERING                                  925 1451
     Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section         925 1451
     from total cross section.                                     925 1451
   SECTION 3.  NON-ELASTIC SCATTERING                              925 1451
     Obtained by setting MT3 =                                     925 1451
             MT4+MT16+MT22+MT28+MT102+MT103+MT104+MT105+MT107.     925 1451
   SECTION 4. TOTAL INELASTIC SCATTERING                           925 1451
     Obtained by summing MT=51-71 and 91.                          925 1451
   SECTION 16. (N,2N) REACTION                                     925 1451
     Calculated by TNG code.                                       925 1451
   SECTION 22. (N,NA)+(N,AN) REACTION                              925 1451
     Calculated by TNG code.                                       925 1451
   SECTION 28. (N,NP)+N,PN) REACTION                               925 1451
     Calculated by TNG code.                                       925 1451
   SECTIONS 51 AND 52. INELASTIC SCATTERING FOR FIRST AND SECOND   925 1451
                       LEVELS                                      925 1451
     Obtained by CS(EX)/MG(TNG), where CS(EX) denotes measured     925 1451
     110 keV and 197 keV gamma-ray production cross section        925 1451
     [MO74], MG(TNG) are multiplicities for 110 and 197 keV        925 1451
     calculated by TNG.                                            925 1451
   SECTIONS 53 - 71. INELASTIC SCATTERING FOR OTHER LEVELS         925 1451
     Calculated by TNG and DWUCK [KU72].                           925 1451
   SECTION 91. CONTINUUM INELASTIC SCATTERING                      925 1451
     Calculated by TNG.                                            925 1451
   SECTION 102. (N,GAMMA) REACTION                                 925 1451
     1.0E-05 eV to 2.0 MeV: Calculated by SAMMY code using a set   925 1451
     of resonance parameters used in the calculation for total     925 1451
     cross sections, but gamma-widths were adjusted to fit the     925 1451
     measured data of Macklin [MA63] and Gabbard [GA59].           925 1451
     Above 2.0 MeV, capture cross sections are very small so 1/E   925 1451
     is used to extrapolate to 20 MeV.                             925 1451
   SECTION 103. (N,P) REACTION                                     925 1451
     For energies < 8.0 MeV, ENDF/B-V remains unchanged.           925 1451
     Above 8.0 MeV: Calculated by TNG code.                        925 1451
   SECTION 104. (N,D) REACTION                                     925 1451
     Calculated from systematics [ZH88].                           925 1451
     The excitation function was normalized to 22 mb given by      925 1451
     integrating early angular distribution data of Fazio [FA68],  925 1451
     and [RE68] at 14 MeV.                                         925 1451
   SECTION 105. (N,T) REACTION                                     925 1451
     Calculated from systematics [ZH88]. The excitation function   925 1451
     was normalized to spectrum averaged measured data of Qaim     925 1451
     [QA78].                                                       925 1451
   SECTION 107. (N,A) REACTION                                     925 1451
     For energies < 9.0 MeV, ENDF/B-V remains unchanged.           925 1451
     Above 9.0 MeV, calculated by TNG code.                        925 1451
 FILE 4. ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY NEUTRONS               925 1451
   SECTION 2. ELASTIC SCATTERING                                   925 1451
     The Legendre coefficients are calculated by the GENOA         925 1451
     optical model code [PE67] with compound cross sections        925 1451
     and Legendre coefficients calculated by TNG as input.         925 1451
     Before calculation, optical model parameters were adjusted    925 1451
     to fit measured angular distributions of Baba [BA85] and      925 1451
     Clarke [CL70]. Same optical model parameters were used in     925 1451
     TNG, DWUCK and GENOA calculations.                            925 1451
   SECTIONS 51-71. INELASTIC SCATTERING                            925 1451
     The cross sections CS(D), Legendre coefficients FL(D)         925 1451
     contributed from direct interaction were calculated by        925 1451
     DWUCK and CS(S), FL(S) are from statistical model by          925 1451
     TNG, using                                                    925 1451
                       CS(D)*FL(D) + CS(S)*FL(S)                   925 1451
                FL = ------------------------------                925 1451
                             CS(D) + CS(S)                         925 1451
 FILE 6. DOUBLE DIFFERENTIAL CROSS SECTIONS(DDCS)                  925 1451
   The cross sections for all sections were obtained based on      925 1451
   TNG calculations for the first outgoing neutrons only.  For     925 1451
   the second outgoing neutrons and both the first and second      925 1451
   outgoing charged particles, the angular distributions were      925 1451
     assumed isotropic. Recoil spectra are generated as the        925 1451
     calculated particle spectra were inverted to the laboratory   925 1451
     system.                                                       925 1451
 FILE 8. RADIOACTIVE DECAY DATA                                    925 1451
 FILE 9. MULTIPLICITIES FOR PRODUCTION OF RADIOACTIVE NUCLIDES     925 1451
 FILE 12. TRANSITION PROBABILITY ARRAYS                            925 1451
   SECTIONS 51-71.                                                 925 1451
     Based on [AJ87].                                              925 1451
 FILE 14. PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTION                              925 1451
   SECTIONS 51-71. INELASTIC SCATTERING                            925 1451
     Isotropic.                                                    925 1451
 FILE 33. UNCERTANTIES OF FILE 3                                   925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
   ENDF/B-VII: Only high quality covariance data were migrated     925 1451
               form ENDF/B-VI.8 (M. Herman)                        925 1451
                                                                   925 1451
   SECTIONS 4,16,22 AND 28:                                        925 1451
     Calculated  from a covariance matrix of theoretical           925 1451
     parameters (several most sensitive parameters were chosen     925 1451
     as follows: energy level density parameters for 19F, 19O      925 1451
     and 16N; optical model parameters for 19F: V0 and W for       925 1451
     real and imaginary well depths, RU and RW for the radius      925 1451
     of real and imaginary potential).  The covariance matrix      925 1451
     for theoretical parameters was estimated based on scatter     925 1451
     of measured data available around theoretical values and      925 1451
     systematic error of measured data. A sub-subsection of LB=8   925 1451
     is also given for every section.                              925 1451
